cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RACER-GT, please cite both the software release and the accompanying methodology manuscript."
title: "RACER-GT: Randomized Acquisition, Calibration, Error Decomposition, and Reliability for Google Trends"
abstract: >-
  A design-based statistical framework and Python package for constructing
  long-horizon daily Google Trends relative-search-interest indices from
  repeated, separately normalized retrievals. It treats data acquisition as a
  preregistered repeated-measurement experiment: global overlap-graph
  calibration replaces sequential stitching, generalizability theory decomposes
  variation across collection days and streams, a covariance-adjusted consensus
  refuses to count dependent retrievals as independent evidence, and the
  resulting measurement uncertainty is propagated into downstream regressions.
